%% One sync session end to end - server change detection by USN journal, cloud change detection by the 24 hour enumeration job, and the failure branches
%% Source: Microsoft Learn "Troubleshoot Azure File Sync sync health and errors" (9102 fields SyncDirection HResult PerItemErrorCount, 9302 progress, change detection job every 24 hours, reconciliation mode, sync blocked until change detection completes after a restore), "Deploy Azure File Sync" (LocalCacheMode), read 2026-09-03; docs/RULES.md AFS-01, AFS-02, AFS-03, AFS-08, SRV-06
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant U as Contoso user on SMB 445
  participant FLT as StorageSync.sys filter driver
  participant SVC as FileSyncSvc on the endpoint server
  participant SSS as Storage Sync Service over the afs private endpoint
  participant SHARE as Azure file share over the file private endpoint
  participant SRV2 as Second server endpoint in the same sync group
  participant OPS as eng-sysops

  Note over U,SHARE: Upload path - a change on the server is detected in minutes
  U->>FLT: write dept budget file over SMB
  FLT->>SVC: NTFS USN journal record
  SVC->>SSS: open upload sync session, send namespace and metadata over HTTPS 443
  SVC->>SHARE: upload the file stream with FileREST over HTTPS 443
  SVC->>SVC: log 9302 progress with TotalItemCount and AppliedItemCount every few minutes
  SSS-->>SVC: session complete
  SVC->>OPS: telemetry 9102 SyncDirection Upload, HResult 0, PerItemErrorCount 0

  Note over SSS,SRV2: Download path - other endpoints learn about it from the service
  SSS->>SRV2: download sync session for the new item
  alt cloud tiering enabled and LocalCacheMode is the default UpdateLocallyCachedFiles
    SRV2->>SRV2: the file appears as a tiered namespace item, content is fetched only on first open
  else LocalCacheMode DownloadNewAndModifiedFiles - proactive recall
    SRV2->>SHARE: recall the full content immediately, paying egress before anyone asks for it
  end

  Note over OPS,SHARE: Cloud path - a change made in the share is NOT detected in minutes
  OPS->>SHARE: copy files straight into the share, or Azure Backup restores an item
  SHARE--)SSS: no change notification exists, Azure Files has no journal
  loop every 24 hours
    SSS->>SHARE: change detection job enumerates every file and compares it to the sync version
  end
  SSS->>SVC: sync session for whatever the enumeration found
  OPS->>SSS: Invoke-AzStorageSyncChangeDetection to force it after a bulk change
  Note over SSS,SHARE: On a large namespace one pass can take longer than 24 hours, and after a restore sync stays blocked until enumeration completes

  Note over SVC,OPS: Failure branches
  alt PerItemErrorCount greater than zero, HResult still 0
    SVC->>OPS: 9121 per item errors - unsupported characters, path over 2048, open handles
    OPS->>SVC: Debug-StorageSyncServer -FileSyncErrorsReport, fix at source, sync retries by itself
  else session HResult non zero
    OPS->>SVC: read the 9102 HResult, then check the storage firewall, DNS and the agent version
    Note over SVC,SSS: watch the Applied counts - rising AppliedFileCount across failing sessions means forward progress, so wait before opening a case
  else ECS_E_REPLICA_RECONCILIATION_NEEDED
    SVC->>SSS: the server was restored to an older state, sync enters reconciliation
    Note over SVC,SHARE: regular sync stops until reconciliation finishes and differing files become conflict files stored side by side
  end
